PMU AWG and PMU DGT used at the same pin
Generating and measuring waveforms in parallel on the same pin is supported by
SmartRDI. For this case, the functions rdi.dc().samples() and rdi.dc().FS() cannot be used
in combination with functions rdi.dc().vMeas() and rdi.dc().iMeas() for setting up the
number of samples or the sample frequency for the measurement:
SmartRDI applies always the number of samples that has been set for the AWG.
The value for the DGT is ignored.
SmartRDI applies always the sample frequency that has been set for the AWG. The
value for the DGT is ignored.
The source code for this approach looks like:
RDI_INIT();
//=====================================================================
//===  PMU AWG and PMU DGT used at the same pin
//=====================================================================
ON_FIRST_INVOCATION_BEGIN();
{
    anaWaveform wav1("sine");
    wav1.definition(TM::SINE).periods(1).samples(256).amplitude(2.0 V).
    rdi.dc().pin("avi_INP")
            .vForce(2.2 V).vForceRange(10.0 V).preCharge(0 V)
            .iClamp(-3.0 mA, 4.5 mA).iForceRange(50 mA)
            .execute();
    RDI_BEGIN();
    {
        rdi.port("port_INP_Force").dc("dig1").pin("avi_INP")
                .vForce().waveform(wav1).FS(250 kHz)
                .vMeas()
                .execute();
    }
    RDI_END();
}
ON_FIRST_INVOCATION_END();

