Note  The example above is programmed as multiport test. The function
rdi.portSync() is to be used to synchronize the forcing pin and the measuring pin
respectively the TMU of the measuring pin: The forcing pin must wait until the setup
of the TMU has been finished and the measuring pin must wait until the forcing pin
has generated the measure signal.
CAUTION The example above is programmed as multiport test. For TMU
measurements SmartRDI places the DC event that stops the TMU measurements.
The END_MEAS event is normally inserted directly after the last action for the related
port. This will result in an incomplete measurement because the last TMU
measurement is stopped before the required signal to be measured has been
generated. The example uses therefore function rdi.port().waitCycle(1) for the
measure port. The waitCycle() is inserted after the last rdi.portSync(). This will
force SmartRDI moving the stop event to a position after the signal to measure has
been generated.
