Example 2: Change current range
The AVI64 PMU current force range and the current measurement range are physically
identical. The difference is the function used in programming:
rdi.dc().iForceRange(): will always change to the programmed target current range.
rdi.dc().iMeasRange(): will use automatic down ranging when changing the current
range.
For defining the rdi.dc().iMeasRange(), the settling time must be considered. The PMU
must not be in clamp current mode if down ranging should be used.
CAUTION Down ranging stops without issuing a warning if down ranging is
started while PMU is clamping the current. This occurs during settling time of the
signal after a force range or force value has been changed.
