Functional changes
Introduced in SmartRDI 2.2.0
Serial/Semi-parallel execution of BADC as
digitizer over sites
Before 2.4.4, SmartRDI does not support the usage of the BADC as digitizer for pins
sharing a BADC over sites.
SmartRDI 2.4.4 supports the usage of BADC as digitizer with serial or semi-parallel
execution in one pattern burst in connection with RDI_SEMI_PARALLEL_TEST_BEGIN()
/RDI_SEMI_PARALLEL_TEST_END().
Both PPMU and BADC-HIZ are supported in this feature.
Example
We assume Pin "DATA36" shares one BADC on sites1 & 2 (pogo 103) and another BADC
on sites 3 & 4 (pogo 104).
Example for a semi-parallel execution of digitizing by BADCs shared over sites. For pin
"DATA36", sites 1 & 3 are executed at first followed by sites 2 & 4. Below are the
example code as well as the code logic illustration.
