RDI_UNIT_INIT()
RDI_UNIT_INIT() is used for conditional code execution. It ensures that the code in an
RDI_UNIT_INIT() block is correctly executed and used for setup generation, even if the
code has been skipped in the first run due to an if-else condition.
For conditional executions, some execute() and rdi.wait() commands may not be
called in each run of a test suite. You need to use RDI_UNIT_INIT() to ensure that
these commands are to be executed.
Syntax
Note  RDI_UNIT_INIT() is required for both pattern‑based and code‑based
commands including pure code‑based commands.
Parameter
Parameter Description
sName A string as an identifier.
For a "live-branch" case, the RDI_UNIT_INIT(string) is for this purpose.
