Offline Result Emulation in SmartRDI
SmartRDI supports Offline Result Emulation (ORE) to evaluate test programs on offline
base.
Offline Result Emulation
ORE supports the usage of defined test results in an emulation file to return these
results in an offline mode.
ORE is commonly used for:
Verifying test programs before a device is available.
Evaluating test programs to detect different types of failures.
In SmartRDI 2.5.0, ORE is supported. You can specify an XML-format ORE file containing
emulation results.
Note  Before using ORE, guarantee that your test program can be executed without
any error.
