Protocols can support burst write and read. The write array operation is performed
through the RA_WRITE_ARRAY() command. The command needs a start address on
which the first array data is written. The address is automatically incremented.
To use write array in your test methods, you must define defineWriteArray() in your
protocol class in advance. For example,
After you have added the definition in your protocol, you can use RA_WRITE_ARRAY() in
your test methods to write array data. See Example 1 below for how to use write array in
test methods.
