SmartCalc (SMC) with SmartRDI
SmartRDI can be used in combination with the SmartCalc (SMC) framework. This allows
you to move time consuming calculations and uploads of test results to separate
background threads and executing them in parallel.
ON_FIRST_INVOCATION_BEGIN();
// Set sites to be on hold and assign labels to these sites.
ARRAY_I holdSites(2);
holdSites[0] = 2;
holdSites[1] = 4;
rdi.setOnHoldSites(holdSites);  
rdi.assignLabelOnHoldSites("holdLabel","pt1");
RDI_BEGIN();
  rdi.port("pt1").smartVec("id1").pin("pinA").writeData()
                                 .pin("pinB").readData().execute();
  rdi.port("pt2").emap()....execute();
RDI_END();
ON_FIRST_INVOCATION_END();
rdi.id("id1").getOnHoldSites(); // Return array_I={2,4}
If(!rdi.id("id1").getOnHoldSitesStatus())
{
      rdi.id("id1").getReadData("pinB"); // Site 1 and site 3 return {x
}
else
{
     // For on hold sites, RDI gives dummy results.
     rdi.id("id1").getReadData("pinB"); // Sites 2 and 4 return{} → dum
}
rdi.clearOnHoldSites(); // Sites 2 and 4 return back to normal state.
