Limitation
When used in the code‑based mode, that is, outside the RDI_BEGIN()/RDI_END()
block, rdi.level().set() or rdi.timing().set() already includes:
Primary.timing()/primary.level()
FLUSH(TM::FLUSH_PRIMARY)
To make the FLUSH action effective for the execution of a test, for example,
FUNCTIONAL_TEST, you must add FLUSH(TM::APRM) after the
rdi.level().set() or rdi.timing().set() relevant commands.
See the code example in Example 3.
When used in the code‑based mode, if the rdi.level().set() or
rdi.timing().set() command is adjacent to a RDI_BEGIN() command, you do not
have to add FLUSH(TM::APRM). The RDI_BEGIN() already includes the
FLUSH(TM::APRM) action. See the code example in Example 2.
