rdi.id().getReadData()
Retrieves all read data blocks and put them into an array of type ARRAY_LL. Usually,
getReadData() is used with rdi.smartVec().readData().
Note  If you set the length of bits to 64 with rdi.smartVec().readData(), for example
readData(64,2), the result returned by getReadData() will be < 0 when bit 64 =
1 due to the long integer value range.
For both TA::EMAP and TA::DIGCAP read modes, the result in ARRAY_LL is the same.
